car tester Reinhold Eisenhower is amazed  at how quickly time flies it's already  been five years since outtie debuted its  new q3 at the time it was the only rival  for BMW x1 in the meantime the lineup of  premium SUVs has grown considerably  Mercedes has enter the race and even  Jaguar has rolled out a premium SUV even  so the q3 series has been a best-seller  for Audi in an effort to build on its  success Audi has given the compact  crossover SUV a facelift we've had they  known that reinholt is going to try out  the dynamic sport and efficiency modes  the suspension can be set to any one of  the three with Drive select the drive  select set ski handling characteristics  according to individual taste for  instance the optional adaptive  suspension it combines nimble handling  with advanced safety features we tested  the most powerful diesel offered for the  q3 with a 135 kilowatt output and an S  tronic 7-speed dual-clutch transmission  on both front and rear horizontal lines  emphasize the q3 s broad shoulders  howdies designers have refined the coupe  eight lines and the characteristically  sleek wraparound tailgate the s-line  sports package on the car we tested made  for a nicely dynamic impression inside  and out the nineteen hundred euro charge  for the trim includes the three spoke  leather sports steering wheel  the seats hug driver and passenger like  those of a racy sports car the back  seats have room for three passengers but  the 460 liters of cargo space is a bit  on the small side remote islands and  plastics reinhold says the engines are  powerful but efficient his only  criticism is that from the side the  taillights look somehow off-kilter but  the well integrated headlights make up  for that in Germany the q3 starts at  about thirty thousand euros the RS q3 is  a bit sportier it's two and a half liter  TFSI engine puts out 250 kilowatts and  leaves from 0 to 100 kilometers an hour  in 4.8 seconds
 

